#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# symmetric_matrix_q

#% text
# `symmetric_matrix_q(m)` gives `true` if the square matrix `m` equals its transpose.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Inexact entries are compared up to rounding.

#% item
# Anything that is not a square matrix gives `false`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
symmetric_matrix_q([[1, 2], [2, 3]])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
symmetric_matrix_q([[1, 2], [3, 3]])
#% output
#= false

#% cell
symmetric_matrix_q([[a, b], [b, c]])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
symmetric_matrix_q([[1, 2, 3], [2, 3, 4]])
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `positive_definite_matrix_q`, `transpose`, `diagonal_matrix_q`
